    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA Beautifully Extended Detached Family Home in a Prime South County Dublin Setting.\n\nA truly special opportunity to acquire a superb four-bedroom detached family home, ideally positioned at the end of a peaceful cul-de-sac in the highly regarded Villarea Park, Glenageary. No. 52 has been carefully modernised and thoughtfully extended by the current owners and now provides approximately c150sqm of bright, well-proportioned accommodation, complemented by an exceptional rear garden.\n\nThe property makes an immediate impression, with a contemporary floor-to-ceiling glazed porch creating a stylish entrance to the home. An inviting hallway leads through to the generous living and dining accommodation, while the superb dual-aspect kitchen extends from the front to the rear of the house and enjoys direct access to the garden through patio doors. The side extension has created an excellent utility room together with a guest WC incorporating a shower, while also providing convenient side access. Upstairs, there are four spacious bedrooms, with the principal bedroom benefiting from an ensuite, alongside a well-appointed family bathroom.\n\nOutside, the rear garden is undoubtedly one of the outstanding features of this home. Exceptionally generous in size and enjoying a wonderful south westerly orientation, it is flooded with natural sunlight and provides an idyllic setting for relaxing, entertaining and family life. The aspect also captures the evening sunshine. A particularly attractive feature is the rear pedestrian access onto The Metals, the renowned pedestrian route extending from Dalkey towards Ballsbridge. The location is exceptional, combining a peaceful residential setting with remarkable convenience. \n\nGlenageary DART Station is just a stone's throw away, while the picturesque villages of Dalkey, Sandycove and Glasthule, together with the seafront, are all within easy reach. Excellent public transport and a superb selection of primary and secondary schools further enhance this highly desirable South County Dublin address."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Special Features</li><li> Four-bedroom detached family home</li><li> Approximately 150sqm</li><li> Beautifully modernised and extended</li><li> Stylish floor-to-ceiling glazed entrance porch</li><li> Generous living and dining accommodation</li><li> Dual-aspect extended kitchen</li><li> Patio doors opening onto the rear garden</li><li> Spacious utility room</li><li> Guest WC with shower</li><li> Convenient side access</li><li> Four well-proportioned bedrooms</li><li> Principal bedroom with ensuite</li><li> Family bathroom</li><li> Exceptionally large landscaped rear garden</li><li> Superb south westerly orientation</li><li> West-facing aspect capturing evening sunshine</li><li> Excellent outdoor entertaining space</li><li> Rear pedestrian access onto The Metals</li><li> Peaceful cul-de-sac setting</li><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Further potential for extension to the rear</li><li> Glenageary DART Station a stone's throw away</li><li> Close to Dalkey, Sandycove and Glasthule</li><li> Short walk to the seafront</li><li> Excellent public transport connections</li><li> Wide choice of excellent schools nearby</li><li> BER Rating: C</ul>"
